            { question: "In The Dark Tower by Stephen King, how does the narrator's final statement serve as direct characterization?", quote: "\"And will I tell you that these three lived happily ever after? I will not, for no one ever does. But there was happiness. And they did live.\"", answers: ["It is a direct characterization of the nature of happiness, rejecting a fairy-tale ideal for a more realistic state of being.", "It directly characterizes the three people as being unhappy.", "It directly characterizes the narrator as a liar.", "It directly characterizes the story as a tragedy with no happiness."], correctAnswer: "It is a direct characterization of the nature of happiness, rejecting a fairy-tale ideal for a more realistic state of being." },
